                <pb facs="0423" n="309" xml:id="pg309"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">875.00/140: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-11T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 11,
                                1924—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 2:06 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>114. Following from Grant-Smith: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Repeat to Department: 51, June 8, 4 p.m. The Prime Minister, War
                            Minister and Commander of Gendarmerie fled to Durazzo today. Some
                            hundreds of armed tribesmen still in Tirana. Local authorities will
                            probably be able to maintain order.</p>
                        <p>Government forces in south routed. Insurgent forces expected to enter
                            Tirana tomorrow.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
